==Appearance==
Razzle & Dazzle's heads are comedy and tragedy masks. Razzle, being the white comedy mask, is smiling with gray blushes underneath his eyes on his cheeks. Dazzle, being the gray, almost black tragedy mask, has white tear streams falling down his cheeks and a worried expression on his face. Both masks are U-shaped, with rounded bottoms and pointed top, sharp edges. 

Their appearance is akin to conjoined twins (specifically fraternal or non-identical twins due to their somewhat different appearances), conjoined by the neck but sharing the same body. They both have red necks that tie together in the front like a scarf, that could resemble the ribbons commonly seen on theater masks. Their outfit consists of a simple, sleeveless black shirt that slightly exposes the bottom of their torso. Moreover, their torso and limbs are split down the middle, with the right leg and arm being white like Razzle and the left leg and arm being gray like Dazzle.

==Personalities==
Razzle and Dazzle both have extremely different personalities, which represent their respective theatre masks.

Razzle is a rather excitable, friendly [[Toon]]. He appears to be eager to spend time with the others, as well as enjoying the spotlight. He states, "Couldn't be better!" when asked about how he's doing, which is reflective of his optimistic, happy personality. He is always bursting with energy, outgoing and very curious about the world. He will always try to defend and stand up for his brother though, and try to cheer up other toons as well.

Dazzle, on the other hand, is a rather gloomy, pessimistic Toon. He appears to have a rather negative outlook and a slightly depressive personality, dismissing positive comments about him. After being complimented by {{CI|Boxten|name=true}}, Dazzle says, "I wish my best was enough..." which further suggests this. He also might be slightly anxious, as in his old extracting animation, he is shown looking nervously to the side. He also shows fear around {{CI|Pebble|name=true}} and {{CI|Coal|name=true}} in his interactions with them. However, he doesn't reach the same degree of distress as {{CI|Squirm|name=true}}, even reacting a bit awkwardly to his outbursts and trying to ease his pessimism. Nevertheless, he is friendly also, and cares about other Toons' well-being, as shown in his dialogue with {{CI|Tisha|name=true}}, where he acts concerned and tells her not to overwork herself.

However, despite being so different, neither twin fights, as described in their dialogue with {{CI|Gigi|name=true}}. Instead being open and accepting of each other in spite of their opposing personalities.

