==Requirement Strategies==
*For the first and only requirement, focus on picking up [[Research Capsules]] and extracting [[Machines]]. The Machine and Capsule count increases the further you descend, so you can earn more {{II|Ichor|name=true}}.

==Strategies==
Razzle & Dazzle have a vacillating playstyle. Their varying [[Stats]] give them great potential, enabling them to demonstrate two extreme builds with their hybrid playstyle of swapping between distracting and extracting. In the following segments, Razzle and Dazzle are referred to as '''Razzle''' when they are on '''odd [[Floors]]''' (speed) and '''Dazzle''' on '''even Floors''' (extraction).

Their Passive [[Ability]] causes the user to swap their strengths between Extraction and Distraction/Survival on Even and Odd Numbered Floors respectively. Razzle's high Movement Speed (5{{Star}}) is perfect for Distracting [[Twisteds]] on odd-numbered Floors or duo distracting with Pebble and other fast toons, and Dazzle's high Extraction Speed is great for Extracting [[Machines]] on even-numbered Floors. The major disadvantage of playing Razzle & Dazzle is Dazzle's extremely low Movement Speed, which is much lower than other similar extractors, and Razzle's subpar Extraction Speed. It's due to this factor that it's recommended to play Razzle & Dazzle on a team as opposed to playing on your own, as Dazzle's speed deficit is often fatal if they're chased by a Twisted, and machines will take approximately 1 minute when on odd floors. Razzle & Dazzle's Ability allows them to assume the most powerful stats of a {{Type|Main}} across each Floor. Their Ability breaks Floors up a little more to make things more exciting, but it comes at a large opportunity cost.

As for [[Items]], Razzle & Dazzle can use anything well. It's recommended to take Healing Items, as those are always generally useful, and to collect Movement Speed/Stamina Items during Razzle's turn to make Dazzle's safer.

The main thing determining Razzle & Dazzle's Ability is their Trinkets. Movement Speed-boosting Trinkets (such as {{TI|Ribbon Spool|name=true}}, {{TI|Clown Horn|name=true}}, etc.) are highly recommended as they can boost their mobility, which is helpful for both, and extraction-boosting Trinkets ({{TI|Vee's Remote|name=true}}, {{TI|Magnifying Glass|name=true}}, etc.) can help them extract nicely. Although there's no best set of Trinkets for Razzle & Dazzle, but it's best to use two speed Trinkets or one movement and one extraction, as this can help flesh out one of their Roles better. It's better to pick Trinkets that synergize with one another. 

Razzle & Dazzle's best support looks like another distractor that handles Dazzle's Floors. If this is the case, the Razzle user may wish to equip Clown Horn and {{TI|Dog Plush|name=true}} and the other Toon can equip Ribbon Spool in place of Clown Horn. While this is a common setup for duo distracting, it comes with the benefits of Razzle & Dazzle's extra heart compared to Pebble and extra Extraction during downtime. Downsides include an extreme lack of survivability if your other distractor dies, an inability to take over/backup distract if they're low on Health, and being devoid of a good way to gather Items downtime normally provides. 

Razzle's speed is sufficient to distract all singular Twisteds (including {{CI|Twisted Pebble|name=true}}, though combinations may get dicey) so their user might opt to instead solely equip Trinkets that benefit Dazzle. 

Overall it is really only recommended to play Razzle & Dazzle if you're experienced and can deal with their constant-changing Statistics.

